###########################
#  Main text

BEGIN_TEXT
Let \( F:\mathbb{R}^3 \to \mathbb{R}^3 \) and \( G : \mathbb{R}^3 \to \mathbb{R}^3 \) be \( C^2 \) vector fields with \( F = (F_1,F_2,F_3) \) and \( G = (G_1,G_2,G_3) \).  Let \( f : \mathbb{R}^3 \to \mathbb{R} \) and \( g : \mathbb{R}^3 \to \mathbb{R} \) be  \( C^2 \) scalar functions. Which statements are true, false, or nonsense?
$BR $BR

1. \( \text{curl}(F)  = \big( \partial_2 F_3 - \partial_3 F_2, \partial_3 F_1 - \partial_1 F_3, \partial_1 F_2 - \partial_2 F_1 \big) \)
END_TEXT

BEGIN_PGML
[@ $radio1->buttons() @]*
END_PGML

BEGIN_TEXT
$BR
2. \( \text{curl}(F) = \nabla \times F \)
END_TEXT

BEGIN_PGML
[@ $radio2->buttons() @]*
END_PGML

BEGIN_TEXT
$BR
3. \( \text{curl}(\nabla f) = 0 \)
END_TEXT

BEGIN_PGML
[@ $radio3->buttons() @]*
END_PGML

BEGIN_TEXT
$BR
4. \( \nabla(\text{curl}(F))  = F \)
END_TEXT

BEGIN_PGML
[@ $radio4->buttons() @]*
END_PGML

BEGIN_TEXT
$BR
5. \( \text{curl}( \text{div}(F) ) = 0 \)
END_TEXT

BEGIN_PGML
[@ $radio5->buttons() @]*
END_PGML

BEGIN_TEXT
$BR
6. \( \text{div}(\text{curl}(F)) = 0 \)
END_TEXT

BEGIN_PGML
[@ $radio6->buttons() @]*
END_PGML

BEGIN_TEXT
$BR
7. \( \text{curl}(F \times G)  = \text{curl}(F) G + F \text{curl}(G) \)
END_TEXT

BEGIN_PGML
[@ $radio7->buttons() @]*
END_PGML

BEGIN_TEXT
$BR
8. \( \text{curl}(F \times F) = 0 \)
END_TEXT

BEGIN_PGML
[@ $radio8->buttons() @]*
END_PGML

